* Stroke within the past 6 months;
* Atrial fibrillation or uncontrolled heart rate (HR) (\> 100 beats per minute \[bpm\]);
* Significant arrhythmia or second or third degree atrio-ventricular block;
* Valvular disease as the primary cause of HF;
* Significant ECG abnormalities as assessed by appropriately qualified physician or investigator including QTcF \>450;
* Positive testing for Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV), Hepatitis B and/or Hepatitis C;

Main randomization exclusion criteria:

* HR \> 100 bpm or \ 5.3 mmol/L or \ 1.1 mmol/L or \ ULN.

Inclusion Criteria:

* Histologically or cytologically confirmed HNSCC (excluding nasopharyngeal carcinoma);
* At least one measurable lesion (spiral CT scan long diameter ≥ 10 mm or enlarged lymph node short diameter ≥ 15 mm by RECIST 1.1);
* Documented disease progression after prior platinum-based systematic therapy; or prior platinum-based adjuvant/neoadjuvant therapy with documented disease progression within 24 weeks after treatment completion;
* Expected overall survival≥ 3 months;
